1
00:00:00,917 --> 00:00:04,754
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:12,637
[Camia] <i>Nimfa got hold of my phone.</i>

3
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:14,556
[Lily] <i>Mom, we've known her for a while,</i>

4
00:00:14,639 --> 00:00:18,018
<i>but we can't just trust her.</i>
<i>We can't take our chances.</i>

5
00:00:18,101 --> 00:00:20,270
<i>Ivy's getting married to Arnaldo.</i>

6
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,730
<i>We can't let that happen.</i>

7
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:24,566
<i>Ivy and Arnaldo are now engaged.</i>

8
00:00:24,649 --> 00:00:26,109
<i>Ivy had better watch out.</i>

9
00:00:26,192 --> 00:00:29,154
<i>She'll regret saying yes to my son.</i>

10
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:31,156
[Nimfa] <i>Don't you ever think</i>

11
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:33,074
<i>that there's someone else</i>
<i>who's better for you?</i>

12
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:35,744
<i>A girl who can really love you?</i>

13
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:39,664
<i>Nimfa, wait. Can we not ruin what we have?</i>

14
00:00:39,748 --> 00:00:42,167
[Emilia] <i>Congratulations</i>
<i>on your engagement, Ivy.</i>

15
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,253
<i>How thoughtful of you, Emilia.</i>
<i>But where's the bride's head?</i>

16
00:00:45,336 --> 00:00:46,880
[clamor]

17
00:00:46,963 --> 00:00:49,799
<i>I'm gonna do everything to ruin</i>
<i>your engagement with my son!</i>

18
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:50,967
<i>Bring it on!</i>

19
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:53,553
[Ivy] <i>I guess Emilia</i>
<i>and I will never get along,</i>

20
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:56,598
<i>so let's just call off the wedding.</i>

21
00:00:56,681 --> 00:00:58,016
[Arnaldo] <i>Don't ever think about that.</i>

22
00:00:58,099 --> 00:01:00,101
<i>I really think</i>
<i>Mom is just feeling insecure.</i>

23
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:02,270
<i>Our family is rich, but she isn't.</i>

24
00:01:02,353 --> 00:01:04,856
<i>She doesn't know where</i>
<i>Grandpa's keeping our money.</i>

25
00:01:04,939 --> 00:01:08,860
<i>Over my dead body, Arnaldo!</i>
<i>I will not apologize to her!</i>

26
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:10,070
<i>That woman will soon be my wife</i>

27
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:11,529
<i>and the future mother of my children.</i>

28
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:14,074
<i>Apologize to her,</i>
<i>or you're going to lose a son,</i>

29
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:15,825
<i>and gain one more enemy on your list.</i>

30
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:17,035
[Ivy] <i>I'm just wondering…</i>

31
00:01:17,118 --> 00:01:21,623
<i>The Ardientes haven't kept their money</i>
<i>in any bank here or overseas.</i>

32
00:01:21,706 --> 00:01:23,917
[Diego] <i>Why are you thinking that?</i>

33
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,961
<i>You're in the home of murderers.</i>
<i>You have to be careful.</i>

34
00:01:27,045 --> 00:01:29,172
[Ivy] <i>If you don't stop</i>
<i>breathing down my neck, Emilia,</i>

35
00:01:29,255 --> 00:01:32,258
<i>I'll take what little you still have left.</i>

36
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:33,760
<i>It won't just stress you out,</i>

37
00:01:33,843 --> 00:01:36,554
<i>you might go into depression too.</i>

38
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:38,681
[huffs]

39
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:42,435
Excuse me?

40
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:47,232
[sighs] Too bad there's no more cake left.

41
00:01:47,315 --> 00:01:48,399
Okay.

42
00:01:55,198 --> 00:01:56,199
Hm.

43
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,496
Good night, my future mother-in-law.

44
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:05,250
[mockingly]
You'll learn to love me someday.

45
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:08,294
[door slams]

46
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:12,465
[tense music playing]

47
00:02:12,549 --> 00:02:13,550
[exhales sharply]

48
00:02:20,849 --> 00:02:27,605
[plaintive music playing]

49
00:02:34,028 --> 00:02:36,030
[Ivy] <i>What are you doing?</i>
<i>It's dangerous here.</i>

50
00:02:36,114 --> 00:02:37,615
[Diego] <i>What you're doing</i>
<i>is far more dangerous.</i>

51
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:39,951
<i>Arnaldo said the Ardientes</i>
<i>have not stashed off their money</i>

52
00:02:40,034 --> 00:02:41,202
<i>in any bank.</i>

53
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:43,997
<i>So I figured it might be here</i>
<i>in the mansion.</i>

54
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,874
<i>Diego, if we find their money,</i>

55
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:48,084
<i>we can take down the Ardientes for good.</i>

56
00:02:48,167 --> 00:02:50,044
[Emilia] <i>I knew it.</i>

57
00:02:50,587 --> 00:02:52,338
[taunting] <i>Hey, Ivy.</i>

58
00:02:53,089 --> 00:02:56,426
<i>I will find you, and I will catch you.</i>

59
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:10,356
<i>Ivy will only put herself in more danger</i>

60
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,900
<i>the longer she stays in that house.</i>

61
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:18,448
[suspenseful music playing]

62
00:03:22,619 --> 00:03:23,828
[door creaks]

63
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:37,091
[suspenseful music swells]

64
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:06,621
[suspenseful music swells]

65
00:04:25,223 --> 00:04:30,561
[suspenseful music continues playing]

66
00:04:30,645 --> 00:04:33,231
[vehicle engine rumbles]

67
00:04:50,707 --> 00:04:55,670
[suspenseful music continues playing]

68
00:05:03,886 --> 00:05:08,016
[vehicle engine rumbles]

69
00:05:13,062 --> 00:05:14,105
[phone rings]

70
00:05:14,814 --> 00:05:15,815
[phone rings]

71
00:05:16,607 --> 00:05:18,985
[phone rings]

72
00:05:20,194 --> 00:05:21,362
Mom?

73
00:05:21,446 --> 00:05:23,656
[sighs] I got to talk to you finally.

74
00:05:24,574 --> 00:05:26,200
<i>I've been worried since last night.</i>

75
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:29,037
I was just about to go to your house.

76
00:05:29,495 --> 00:05:32,790
<i>-Let's meet up somewhere.</i>
-All right. I'll be there.

77
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:35,877
-I'll see you, Mom.
-Okay.

78
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:45,219
[ominous music playing]

79
00:05:48,222 --> 00:05:51,100
-Oh, hey. Good morning.
-Hi! Good morning.

80
00:05:51,184 --> 00:05:53,144
I got here just in time.
Let me drive you home.

81
00:05:53,227 --> 00:05:56,022
Um, I already had my driver
pick me up. But thank you.

82
00:05:56,105 --> 00:05:59,358
-Just see me out.
-Okay, I will.

83
00:06:01,235 --> 00:06:03,154
-Take care today, okay?
-You too.

84
00:06:03,237 --> 00:06:05,531
-I'll miss you.
-I'll miss you more.

85
00:06:13,122 --> 00:06:14,373
[phone rings]

86
00:06:15,374 --> 00:06:16,292
Hello?

87
00:06:16,375 --> 00:06:17,960
Camia's meeting with someone.

88
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:19,504
<i>I bet it's someone important.</i>

89
00:06:19,587 --> 00:06:20,963
She was in a hurry.

90
00:06:21,047 --> 00:06:23,091
It might be the person helping her?

91
00:06:23,174 --> 00:06:24,759
It might be Ivy Aguas.

92
00:06:24,842 --> 00:06:26,344
She was here at the mansion,

93
00:06:26,427 --> 00:06:28,429
<i>and she left in a hurry too.</i>

94
00:06:28,513 --> 00:06:29,347
<i>Anyway,</i>

95
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:30,181
this is what you'll do.

96
00:06:30,264 --> 00:06:31,849
You follow Camia,

97
00:06:31,933 --> 00:06:34,060
while I follow Ivy Aguas.

98
00:06:35,269 --> 00:06:36,646
Okay, bye.

99
00:06:41,025 --> 00:06:45,029
[suspenseful music playing]

100
00:07:09,053 --> 00:07:10,680
[suspenseful music continues playing]

101
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:27,822
[suspenseful music swells]

102
00:07:37,039 --> 00:07:40,334
[suspenseful music intensifies]

103
00:07:57,977 --> 00:07:59,479
[elevator bell pings]

104
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:37,266
-Stay here. Don't follow me.
-Yes, ma'am.

105
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:48,694
[suspenseful music continues playing]

106
00:08:53,032 --> 00:08:56,327
This time, Auntie Claire,
we'll see for ourselves

107
00:08:56,410 --> 00:08:59,872
just what Ivy Aguas' ties
to Camia Cruz really are.

108
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:03,209
Let's go. Let the hunt begin.

109
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:25,731
[suspenseful music playing]

110
00:09:53,676 --> 00:09:57,346
[suspenseful music continues playing]

111
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:13,362
[suspenseful music swells]

112
00:10:43,476 --> 00:10:47,480
[suspenseful music continues playing]

113
00:10:49,273 --> 00:10:50,441
-Oh, hi!
-Hi, you're here.

114
00:10:50,524 --> 00:10:52,526
Remember me? I'm Ivy Aguas.

115
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:53,736
-Yes.
-Hello.

116
00:10:54,195 --> 00:10:56,364
-Hi. Nice to meet you.
-You too.

117
00:10:59,325 --> 00:11:00,451
Yes, ma'am?

118
00:11:01,327 --> 00:11:07,041
Um… Miss, have you seen
a lady with two bodyguards?

119
00:11:07,124 --> 00:11:09,710
No, ma'am. Try checking
with the next store.

120
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:12,963
So, um…

121
00:11:14,548 --> 00:11:16,425
-Is everything set?
-Yes, ma'am.

122
00:11:16,509 --> 00:11:18,469
Sorry, I hope I'm not disturbing anything.

123
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:23,599
Actually, I'm waiting for someone.

124
00:11:29,814 --> 00:11:31,565
[waitress] Have you placed
your order, ma'am?

125
00:11:34,652 --> 00:11:36,320
Anything else, ma'am? All right.

126
00:11:36,695 --> 00:11:38,197
If you need anything else, just say so.

127
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,281
Okay.

128
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:43,619
-She'll be here soon, I hope.
-[woman] Okay.

129
00:11:43,702 --> 00:11:46,705
[tense music playing]

130
00:11:53,379 --> 00:11:56,382
-Are we waiting for anyone else?
-Who are you expecting, ma'am?

131
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:01,303
Anyway, I have to go.

132
00:12:01,387 --> 00:12:02,805
-Again, nice meeting you.
-Thank you.

133
00:12:02,888 --> 00:12:04,598
-Nice to see you, bye.
-Thank you.

134
00:12:04,682 --> 00:12:07,518
[suspenseful music playing]

135
00:12:35,588 --> 00:12:38,340
-Did you see anyone follow you?
-No, Lily.

136
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:40,843
Mom…

137
00:12:46,307 --> 00:12:49,894
[upbeat music playing]

138
00:13:02,364 --> 00:13:03,324
-Hey!
-Hey!

139
00:13:03,407 --> 00:13:07,203
-Watch where you're going.
-[motorcycle engine rumbles]

140
00:13:09,747 --> 00:13:12,791
<i>Arnaldo is the key to finding out</i>

141
00:13:12,875 --> 00:13:14,919
<i>where they're hiding the money.</i>

142
00:13:15,669 --> 00:13:21,008
<i>But if I'm going to follow him,</i>
<i>I can't use this car.</i>

143
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:32,520
-[jeep door slams]
-[jeep engine rumbles]

144
00:13:35,105 --> 00:13:36,232
He's here, Mayor.

145
00:13:37,816 --> 00:13:39,527
Yes, Grandpa? You called for me?

146
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:41,278
Yes, Arnaldo.

147
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:46,367
I want you to store this money
in our vault.

148
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:47,618
[bills rustling]

149
00:13:47,701 --> 00:13:50,287
It's from Jaguar.

150
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:54,667
It seems like this small fry
wants to impress me.

151
00:13:54,750 --> 00:13:58,045
[scoffs] Who knew Jaguar
was a generous man?

152
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:00,130
All right. I'll do it, Grandpa.

153
00:14:01,173 --> 00:14:04,051
Remember, Arnaldo,
that money is very important

154
00:14:04,134 --> 00:14:06,887
because we will use it for the elections.

155
00:14:08,305 --> 00:14:11,267
Don't worry, I'll guard it
with all my life.

156
00:14:12,893 --> 00:14:14,436
Santos, take this.

157
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:20,025
-We're going now, Grandpa.
-Okay.

158
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:28,742
I'm really sorry, Mom.

159
00:14:29,034 --> 00:14:32,246
I'm sorry if we can only see
each other this way.

160
00:14:32,329 --> 00:14:35,082
That we have to keep it a secret.

161
00:14:35,165 --> 00:14:37,918
But we have to do this, Mom.

162
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:40,921
Because Emilia has been
keeping an eye on me.

163
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:42,464
I don't want her to ruin my plans.

164
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:46,844
I understand, Lily. But
I'm really worried about you.

165
00:14:48,053 --> 00:14:50,222
What you're doing is very dangerous.

166
00:14:53,183 --> 00:14:56,812
[suspenseful music playing]

167
00:14:56,896 --> 00:14:59,815
[motorcycle engine rumbling]

168
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:07,031
[suspenseful music swells]

169
00:15:49,782 --> 00:15:54,453
[suspenseful music continues playing]

170
00:16:27,111 --> 00:16:32,533
[suspenseful music continues playing]

171
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:17,703
I'm sorry, Mom.

172
00:17:18,829 --> 00:17:20,956
But I've still got everything
under control.

173
00:17:21,498 --> 00:17:23,250
So you don't have to worry.

174
00:17:25,586 --> 00:17:29,131
You can't blame me for worrying, Lily.

175
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:31,258
Especially since you've reached the point

176
00:17:31,341 --> 00:17:33,343
of faking a relationship with the enemy.

177
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:37,222
[plaintive music playing]

178
00:17:39,141 --> 00:17:43,270
Mom, my relationship
with Arnaldo is all for show.

179
00:17:43,353 --> 00:17:47,483
Everything is a lie.
It's all just part of my plan.

180
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:50,903
Maybe for you, but not for him.

181
00:17:51,445 --> 00:17:54,531
Men like him are dangerous
when they get obsessed.

182
00:17:54,615 --> 00:17:58,285
I've experienced it firsthand
with his father, Raul.

183
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:00,662
I know that, Mom.

184
00:18:03,665 --> 00:18:06,460
But entering a relationship with Arnaldo

185
00:18:06,543 --> 00:18:10,631
is the easiest way
to infiltrate the Ardientes.

186
00:18:10,714 --> 00:18:14,927
Emilia's growing more suspicious
of me by the day,

187
00:18:15,010 --> 00:18:20,057
and I know the congressman
hasn't trusted me since day one.

188
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:25,354
But Arnaldo? I've got him
wrapped around my finger.

189
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:28,190
He's fallen hard for me, Mom.

190
00:18:28,273 --> 00:18:30,234
I've got him right where I want him.

191
00:18:31,068 --> 00:18:34,446
How far will this go, Lily?
Until you end up marrying him?

192
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:38,450
Of course not.
I won't let it get that far.

193
00:18:40,410 --> 00:18:42,913
Diego's helping me, Mom.

194
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:47,000
If his plan succeeds,

195
00:18:47,084 --> 00:18:49,920
I have no doubt we can finally
take down the Ardientes.

196
00:18:53,257 --> 00:18:57,678
[dramatic music playing]

197
00:19:04,476 --> 00:19:06,979
[camera shutter clicking]

198
00:19:11,567 --> 00:19:14,361
<i>Looks like this is where</i>
<i>they're hiding the money.</i>

199
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:25,581
[motorcycle engine revs]

200
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:28,792
I know you're worried, Mom.

201
00:19:31,128 --> 00:19:35,299
And I'm sorry for making you
go through this every day.

202
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:39,094
I'm always praying for you.

203
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:41,597
And don't forget that
I'm always here for you.

204
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:45,517
Especially now that Emilia's
fighting you head-on.

205
00:19:47,019 --> 00:19:48,687
You have to watch out for her.

206
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:52,441
I'm worried that Emilia
might get desperate

207
00:19:52,524 --> 00:19:54,818
and force you to do the unthinkable.

208
00:19:54,902 --> 00:19:59,072
She can try, Mom. But I won't let her.

209
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:04,286
We used to be helpless
against the Ardientes,

210
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:07,748
but now we can hold our own against them.

211
00:20:07,831 --> 00:20:11,043
I was just a weak little girl
back then, Mom.

212
00:20:12,002 --> 00:20:15,547
But now, I will use everything
Miss Prianka taught me…

213
00:20:16,131 --> 00:20:18,425
against the Ardientes.

214
00:20:23,138 --> 00:20:27,976
Lily, promise me that you won't get hurt.

215
00:20:29,561 --> 00:20:30,687
Because I can never bear

216
00:20:30,771 --> 00:20:32,856
the mere thought of you getting hurt.

217
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:35,692
You're the only one I have left.

218
00:20:37,236 --> 00:20:38,612
I promise, Mom…

219
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:43,951
I promise you that
nothing will tear us apart.

220
00:20:44,701 --> 00:20:46,453
Nothing will separate us again.

221
00:20:47,371 --> 00:20:48,956
I promise, Mom.

222
00:20:55,462 --> 00:20:58,757
[suspenseful music playing]

223
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:04,471
[Emilia] I have no patience for
Ivy, Aunt Claire.

224
00:21:05,430 --> 00:21:08,308
I have to resort back to my old tricks.

225
00:21:09,935 --> 00:21:11,186
Old tricks?

226
00:21:12,604 --> 00:21:15,065
Like what you did to Camia Cruz?

227
00:21:15,148 --> 00:21:18,402
[scoffs] Yes. Exactly, Auntie.

228
00:21:21,738 --> 00:21:22,698
[henchman] Ma'am.

229
00:21:24,074 --> 00:21:26,827
[suspenseful music playing]

230
00:21:26,910 --> 00:21:28,662
Welcome, boys!

231
00:21:29,746 --> 00:21:31,707
Are you ready for your new assignment?

232
00:21:32,165 --> 00:21:34,209
-Yes, ma'am.
-Good.

233
00:21:42,050 --> 00:21:43,176
[Raul] Papa.

234
00:21:44,428 --> 00:21:45,762
I let myself in, sorry.

235
00:21:48,348 --> 00:21:49,433
Uh…

236
00:21:53,770 --> 00:21:55,939
Relax, Papa. I'm not going to do anything.

237
00:21:56,023 --> 00:21:58,942
I… I just came here to talk to you.

238
00:22:00,152 --> 00:22:01,278
You know what, Raul?

239
00:22:01,361 --> 00:22:03,572
If there's one thing that I'll never do…

240
00:22:04,406 --> 00:22:08,201
that is to let my guard down
when you're around.

241
00:22:08,952 --> 00:22:10,746
What do you think of me? Stupid?

242
00:22:10,829 --> 00:22:11,830
[scoffs]

243
00:22:11,913 --> 00:22:13,749
Do you know what you remind me of?

244
00:22:14,374 --> 00:22:16,043
A mad dog.

245
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:20,797
The type that just sits in one corner,

246
00:22:20,881 --> 00:22:22,466
pretending to be calm,

247
00:22:22,549 --> 00:22:24,843
-[snickers] mouth drooling…
-[scoffs]

248
00:22:24,926 --> 00:22:29,347
but waiting to strike at any moment.

249
00:22:30,098 --> 00:22:31,433
That's the way I see you.

250
00:22:31,767 --> 00:22:34,227
Fine. You can say anything
you want to say about me.

251
00:22:34,311 --> 00:22:37,064
You can say I'm like a mad dog.

252
00:22:37,147 --> 00:22:39,733
-I can be, sometimes.
-[Julio scoffs]

253
00:22:39,816 --> 00:22:43,278
If only to prove how much
I love your daughter, Emilia.

254
00:22:43,862 --> 00:22:45,655
And that's the only reason I came here.

255
00:22:46,656 --> 00:22:49,576
With all due respect,
I'm asking for your permission.

256
00:22:50,869 --> 00:22:51,953
If it's all right with you,

257
00:22:52,037 --> 00:22:54,664
I'd like to marry your daughter
for a second time.

258
00:22:54,748 --> 00:22:55,707
[scoffs]

259
00:22:55,791 --> 00:22:59,169
[cackles]

260
00:23:05,175 --> 00:23:06,176
Oh!

261
00:23:06,843 --> 00:23:09,596
[wheezing laughter]

262
00:23:10,847 --> 00:23:12,641
Raul… [laughs uncontrollably]

263
00:23:12,724 --> 00:23:14,017
I'll give it to you.

264
00:23:14,101 --> 00:23:17,687
That was the funniest joke
I've ever heard in…

265
00:23:18,313 --> 00:23:20,649
in forever!

266
00:23:20,732 --> 00:23:25,862
Why don't you work as a carnival
clown or a court jester?

267
00:23:25,946 --> 00:23:28,365
Who knows? Making people
laugh might be your calling.

268
00:23:28,824 --> 00:23:30,575
[hoots and laughs]

269
00:23:30,659 --> 00:23:33,203
I have no plans of making
other people happy.

270
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:37,165
I only want to make
your daughter, Emilia, happy.

271
00:23:37,249 --> 00:23:40,919
[wheezing laughter]

272
00:23:41,795 --> 00:23:46,633
[wheezes and coughs]

273
00:23:46,716 --> 00:23:50,428
-Papa… Papa, are you okay?
-[wheezing laughter]

274
00:23:50,512 --> 00:23:53,306
-Don't laugh too much, okay?
-[exaggerated heaving]

275
00:23:53,390 --> 00:23:56,476
It's not good for you. You could
die from a heart attack!

276
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:58,770
-[wheezing laughter]
-Look…

277
00:23:58,854 --> 00:24:01,940
Come to think of it, if you die,

278
00:24:02,023 --> 00:24:04,359
you'd at least die happy,
because you died laughing.

279
00:24:05,485 --> 00:24:08,989
[coughing] What did you say?

280
00:24:09,322 --> 00:24:12,242
See? You've gone deaf too.

281
00:24:12,325 --> 00:24:15,745
-Go on, Raul. Mock me!
-I'm not doing that.

282
00:24:15,829 --> 00:24:19,416
-Mock me as much as you want.
-No. I won't do that.

283
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:21,960
But this I can assure you.

284
00:24:22,836 --> 00:24:24,796
My daughter already made the mistake

285
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:28,049
of marrying a loser like you once.

286
00:24:28,967 --> 00:24:31,887
And I don't think my daughter

287
00:24:31,970 --> 00:24:36,016
will make that mistake
twice in her lifetime.

288
00:24:37,225 --> 00:24:40,812
Come to think of it, if I was
given the chance to choose,

289
00:24:41,855 --> 00:24:45,192
I'd rather let my daughter marry that…

290
00:24:45,275 --> 00:24:48,403
that bastard, Jaguar! [laughing]

291
00:24:48,486 --> 00:24:51,615
At least Jaguar has money.

292
00:24:51,698 --> 00:24:53,575
Okay, that's all.

293
00:25:02,083 --> 00:25:03,251
[door closes]

294
00:25:04,294 --> 00:25:09,382
Could it be true that
Raul's turning over a new leaf?

295
00:25:11,801 --> 00:25:14,095
Nah! Can't be.

296
00:25:18,558 --> 00:25:19,851
[line ringing]

297
00:25:20,644 --> 00:25:21,478
Hello.

298
00:25:22,729 --> 00:25:23,897
Proceed with the plan.

299
00:25:24,481 --> 00:25:26,733
[mahjong tiles rustling]

300
00:25:27,692 --> 00:25:32,239
[suspenseful music playing]

301
00:25:49,297 --> 00:25:50,382
Who are you?!

302
00:25:51,174 --> 00:25:52,259
-[gunshot]
-Get down!

303
00:25:52,342 --> 00:25:57,430
-Hands in the air!
-No! No! Don't!

304
00:25:59,808 --> 00:26:01,935
We are Jaguar's men!

305
00:26:02,519 --> 00:26:04,980
From now on, we'll be taking over

306
00:26:05,063 --> 00:26:09,901
all of Julio Ardiente's gambling
operations. Is that clear?!

307
00:26:10,443 --> 00:26:11,736
Gather all the money.

308
00:26:21,913 --> 00:26:22,831
Let's go.

309
00:26:27,794 --> 00:26:31,256
Um… Ma'am Governor, I'm really sorry.

310
00:26:31,339 --> 00:26:36,052
<i>Everything happened so fast.</i>
<i>She was gone before I knew it.</i>

311
00:26:36,136 --> 00:26:39,097
Well, Nimfa, just make sure

312
00:26:39,180 --> 00:26:41,766
that she doesn't know
she's being followed, okay?

313
00:26:41,850 --> 00:26:43,852
Of course, she doesn't.
She can't possibly know.

314
00:26:43,935 --> 00:26:45,312
You better make sure, because you know

315
00:26:45,395 --> 00:26:47,939
what will happen to you
if Camia finds out…

316
00:26:48,023 --> 00:26:49,232
<i>that you're following her.</i>

317
00:26:50,108 --> 00:26:52,444
Don't you dare push me.

318
00:26:52,861 --> 00:26:55,196
Well, you're a feisty one, aren't you?

319
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:57,490
I just know how to play
my cards, just like you.

320
00:26:57,574 --> 00:27:00,952
Then get your act together, dear.

321
00:27:01,036 --> 00:27:02,871
And do your job properly.

322
00:27:03,455 --> 00:27:06,916
If you want to keep your head.
You know what I can do.

323
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:21,097
I'm sure this funeral parlor
is just a front.

324
00:27:23,308 --> 00:27:26,061
-Ivy, I'm going to break in.
-Diego, don't.

325
00:27:27,062 --> 00:27:28,355
<i>We have to make sure…</i>

326
00:27:28,438 --> 00:27:29,939
what's inside first.

327
00:27:30,398 --> 00:27:33,568
We might find some important evidence.

328
00:27:34,152 --> 00:27:36,279
That will pin down the Ardientes.

329
00:27:37,030 --> 00:27:38,114
Exactly.

330
00:27:39,199 --> 00:27:40,617
And Diego, I just thought…

331
00:27:40,700 --> 00:27:42,869
<i>you should focus on the campaign.</i>

332
00:27:43,370 --> 00:27:44,371
All right, Ivy.

333
00:27:44,454 --> 00:27:46,289
The filing date is coming up soon.

334
00:27:46,373 --> 00:27:48,249
Aunt Camia and I will come up with a plan.

335
00:27:49,376 --> 00:27:51,628
I also want to thank you for everything.

336
00:27:52,545 --> 00:27:53,922
Anything for you.

337
00:27:54,923 --> 00:27:58,676
You stayed up all night
investigating. Again, thank you.

338
00:27:58,760 --> 00:27:59,969
[Arnaldo] Ivy, who's that?

339
00:28:08,853 --> 00:28:10,605
Who were you talking to?

340
00:28:11,689 --> 00:28:17,570
[tense music swells]

341
00:28:18,196 --> 00:28:20,740
[sighs] A representative from
Aguas Realty.

342
00:28:25,620 --> 00:28:27,163
It's about some business in Manila.

343
00:28:27,247 --> 00:28:29,499
They ran into some problems
because I wasn't there.

344
00:28:31,042 --> 00:28:32,043
Hi.

345
00:28:36,965 --> 00:28:38,216
What's with that look?

346
00:28:39,718 --> 00:28:41,344
Are you getting jealous again?

347
00:28:42,429 --> 00:28:44,264
Arnaldo, we already talked about
how I don't want

348
00:28:44,347 --> 00:28:45,974
a partner who's the jealous type.

349
00:28:48,184 --> 00:28:50,937
What are you implying? Not you too!

350
00:28:51,354 --> 00:28:53,481
Your mom is already suspicious of me,

351
00:28:53,565 --> 00:28:55,942
and now you're doubting me too?

352
00:28:56,025 --> 00:28:58,695
Arnaldo, please! Can you please trust me?

353
00:28:58,778 --> 00:28:59,779
How can I trust you?

354
00:28:59,863 --> 00:29:02,073
I was just asking who you were talking to.

355
00:29:02,490 --> 00:29:04,325
I have no idea why you and Mom
are always fighting,

356
00:29:04,409 --> 00:29:06,411
or why she's always suspicious of you.

357
00:29:06,494 --> 00:29:09,497
I was just asking
who you were talking to, okay?

358
00:29:09,581 --> 00:29:11,750
I'm sorry if I upset you!

359
00:29:11,833 --> 00:29:13,334
Why wouldn't I be upset?!

360
00:29:13,877 --> 00:29:15,420
I know that you're doubting me even though

361
00:29:15,503 --> 00:29:17,589
I was simply talking
to someone from Aguas Realty.

362
00:29:17,672 --> 00:29:19,758
I'm having a problem with my business.

363
00:29:21,384 --> 00:29:23,553
-Okay. Fine, fine, fine.
-Please. I don't like this!

364
00:29:23,636 --> 00:29:25,138
Fine, fine. Fine!

365
00:29:25,221 --> 00:29:28,683
How can I not react? You look
at me like you're doubting me.

366
00:29:28,767 --> 00:29:32,604
I'm sorry. I'm sorry if I upset you.

367
00:29:32,687 --> 00:29:34,522
It… it was just a question.

368
00:29:36,107 --> 00:29:40,028
Okay, I-- I think the only way
we can fix this…

369
00:29:40,904 --> 00:29:42,822
is for you to have dinner with my mom.

370
00:29:44,157 --> 00:29:47,243
Okay? So we can fix this
problem once and for all.

371
00:29:49,204 --> 00:29:50,205
[sighs]

372
00:29:51,581 --> 00:29:52,707
Hon…

373
00:29:54,042 --> 00:29:56,294
Of course. I'll do it for you.

374
00:29:57,045 --> 00:30:00,215
Yes. I'll have dinner with your mom.

375
00:30:00,298 --> 00:30:03,009
But the question is, is she ready too?

376
00:30:04,844 --> 00:30:05,845
Yeah.

377
00:30:06,805 --> 00:30:09,349
Yeah, she's ready. It's okay.

378
00:30:09,432 --> 00:30:11,392
She said she has an appointment tomorrow,

379
00:30:11,476 --> 00:30:13,478
so that should be fine.

380
00:30:15,355 --> 00:30:19,025
That's… that's great.
See? Problem solved, then.

381
00:30:20,193 --> 00:30:21,402
[giggles]

382
00:30:26,157 --> 00:30:27,325
Hon…

383
00:30:28,701 --> 00:30:32,705
I don't want us to fight.
Don't be jealous, okay?

384
00:30:33,706 --> 00:30:35,875
You know you're the only one
I love, right?

385
00:30:37,043 --> 00:30:38,378
I love you.

386
00:30:40,004 --> 00:30:41,339
Do you love me?

387
00:30:43,174 --> 00:30:44,968
Yeah. I love you.

388
00:30:46,344 --> 00:30:47,720
-Yeah.
-You love me?

389
00:30:48,388 --> 00:30:50,557
I do. I do.

390
00:30:52,475 --> 00:30:54,185
[coos] Thanks, hon.

391
00:31:03,027 --> 00:31:04,028
Mom.

392
00:31:04,612 --> 00:31:06,239
-Ah, yes?
-Good news.

393
00:31:06,322 --> 00:31:08,533
Ivy agreed to have dinner with you.

394
00:31:08,950 --> 00:31:11,202
Wow. That's really great, son.

395
00:31:11,286 --> 00:31:14,539
Don't worry. After the dinner,
this will all be over.

396
00:31:15,415 --> 00:31:16,958
-I hope so.
-Yeah.

397
00:31:17,041 --> 00:31:19,043
-All right. I'll be going now.
-All right.

398
00:31:34,142 --> 00:31:35,143
[Rufo] Listen up.

399
00:31:35,685 --> 00:31:39,230
Jaguar has a message for us. Watch.

400
00:31:46,529 --> 00:31:48,907
[distorted voice]
<i>Welcome. Welcome to my group.</i>

401
00:31:50,408 --> 00:31:52,535
<i>I'm glad that we're one family now.</i>

402
00:31:53,661 --> 00:31:58,166
<i>As your leader, I will be</i>
<i>generous, unlike Julio.</i>

403
00:31:59,334 --> 00:32:03,212
<i>I want to assure you</i>
<i>that we're all equals here.</i>

404
00:32:04,088 --> 00:32:08,426
<i>Everyone has a fair chance</i>
<i>of becoming king.</i>

405
00:32:09,260 --> 00:32:12,138
<i>Money, women, everything,</i>

406
00:32:12,221 --> 00:32:14,766
<i>I will give everything to each</i>
<i>and every one of you.</i>

407
00:32:15,600 --> 00:32:17,769
<i>But I have just one thing</i>
<i>to ask in return.</i>

408
00:32:18,853 --> 00:32:23,858
<i>You must not walk out</i>
<i>or betray the organization.</i>

409
00:32:23,942 --> 00:32:26,194
<i>That way, everyone will be happy, right?</i>

410
00:32:26,277 --> 00:32:27,737
You're going down, Jaguar!

411
00:32:27,820 --> 00:32:29,530
The congressman will bring you down!

412
00:32:29,614 --> 00:32:31,699
Don't! I'll deal with him.

413
00:32:34,202 --> 00:32:36,871
Stop right there! I won't hurt you.

414
00:32:37,747 --> 00:32:40,416
[grunting]

415
00:32:41,209 --> 00:32:44,045
When Congressman learns about
this, there will be hell to pay!

416
00:32:44,671 --> 00:32:46,881
[grunts and groans]

417
00:32:47,256 --> 00:32:50,259
The next time you try
to escape, I'll finish you off.

418
00:32:55,014 --> 00:32:59,018
Mayor, Congressman, we'll have
a live band and street party,

419
00:32:59,102 --> 00:33:01,187
so we can attract the young voters too.

420
00:33:01,854 --> 00:33:03,523
We will also be holding
a fireworks display

421
00:33:03,606 --> 00:33:05,024
as you announce your candidacy.

422
00:33:05,441 --> 00:33:08,987
And how much is this package
gonna cost us?

423
00:33:09,195 --> 00:33:11,781
Around 10 million for
the event alone, Congressman.

424
00:33:11,864 --> 00:33:13,032
Ten million?

425
00:33:14,033 --> 00:33:16,077
Pretty fair price.

426
00:33:17,328 --> 00:33:20,289
Anyway, I've heard enough. You can go.

427
00:33:20,373 --> 00:33:21,541
Thank you very much, Mr. Congressman.

428
00:33:21,624 --> 00:33:22,709
-Thank you for coming.
-Thank you, Mayor.

429
00:33:25,044 --> 00:33:26,295
[sighs]

430
00:33:29,340 --> 00:33:34,887
Arnaldo, I'm sure Ivy
can sponsor this event for you.

431
00:33:34,971 --> 00:33:37,890
Uh, Grandpa, if it's all right,
let's leave Ivy out of this.

432
00:33:38,766 --> 00:33:39,559
Hmm?

433
00:33:39,642 --> 00:33:42,020
I don't want her to think
that we're only after her money,

434
00:33:42,103 --> 00:33:43,938
or that we're just using her.

435
00:33:45,565 --> 00:33:50,445
But it's the truth, right?
You're only after her money.

436
00:33:51,237 --> 00:33:54,615
Actually, no. Not anymore.
I… I care for her.

437
00:33:54,699 --> 00:34:00,204
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!
Hold your horses, young man.

438
00:34:00,705 --> 00:34:03,750
You can't fall in love with that woman.

439
00:34:04,417 --> 00:34:07,045
I can. I'm already in love with her.

440
00:34:07,920 --> 00:34:11,591
It's just that I can still
be smart at the same time.

441
00:34:13,342 --> 00:34:15,178
Okay. It's your choice.

442
00:34:16,179 --> 00:34:19,057
But I'm telling you, if this goes south…

443
00:34:19,682 --> 00:34:21,100
I'm pulling the plug.

444
00:34:22,226 --> 00:34:23,936
Not just on your dreams…

445
00:34:24,896 --> 00:34:27,857
but also on the life of that
woman you're pining over.

446
00:34:29,567 --> 00:34:31,652
Okay. Challenge accepted.

447
00:34:33,362 --> 00:34:36,032
Okay. Here we go.

448
00:34:41,162 --> 00:34:43,748
I'm sure that the upcoming
election will be a dirty one.

449
00:34:44,290 --> 00:34:47,043
And I know that the Ardientes
won't accept defeat.

450
00:34:47,543 --> 00:34:49,879
That's why we have to be ready
for anything.

451
00:34:51,089 --> 00:34:53,841
We're ready to take them on.

452
00:34:53,925 --> 00:34:56,052
I have faith that Diego will win.

453
00:34:56,803 --> 00:35:00,056
They will not take away Diego's victory.

454
00:35:02,975 --> 00:35:04,477
Okay, good. Let's win this.

455
00:35:05,144 --> 00:35:07,230
We need to prepare a huge event

456
00:35:07,313 --> 00:35:08,940
in time for the filing of your candidacy.

457
00:35:09,315 --> 00:35:11,067
Something that will shock the Ardientes.

458
00:35:13,277 --> 00:35:14,403
[Camia] I have an idea.

459
00:35:14,946 --> 00:35:18,407
When Diego files for candidacy,
his supporters should be there.

460
00:35:19,826 --> 00:35:22,745
Let's see if it doesn't stress
the Ardientes out.

461
00:35:23,121 --> 00:35:24,539
[Marlon] That's good, Miss Camia.

462
00:35:24,622 --> 00:35:25,790
She's right, Diego.

463
00:35:25,873 --> 00:35:29,252
As early as now, we should gain
the support of important people.

464
00:35:29,877 --> 00:35:31,963
We'll need their influence.

465
00:35:34,590 --> 00:35:35,842
I'll take care of that.

466
00:35:37,135 --> 00:35:39,720
I'll make sure that
our first mobilization effort

467
00:35:39,804 --> 00:35:41,514
will be full of people.

468
00:35:52,900 --> 00:35:55,194
-Hi, Papa, Arnaldo.
-Hi, Emilia.

469
00:35:55,570 --> 00:35:57,238
Good that you two are here.

470
00:35:57,947 --> 00:35:59,824
I heard the news, Papa.

471
00:35:59,907 --> 00:36:02,160
I heard that Camia Cruz
is mobilizing people

472
00:36:02,243 --> 00:36:04,745
for Diego's filing of candidacy.

473
00:36:04,829 --> 00:36:06,330
And we have to stop that.

474
00:36:07,915 --> 00:36:10,042
Arnaldo will be on top of that.

475
00:36:10,543 --> 00:36:14,297
[sighs] You know, Emilia, you surprise me.

476
00:36:14,380 --> 00:36:16,507
Where do you get all that information?

477
00:36:17,049 --> 00:36:19,927
Well, Papa, I'm resourceful like you.

478
00:36:20,636 --> 00:36:22,513
Good job. Keep it up.

479
00:36:22,597 --> 00:36:25,975
Um, Papa, Arnaldo,
I'll leave you two here, okay?

480
00:36:26,058 --> 00:36:28,769
I'll just prepare for my dinner with Ivy.

481
00:36:28,853 --> 00:36:31,397
-Okay.
-Oh, by the way.

482
00:36:31,480 --> 00:36:34,275
Please do keep that woman distracted.

483
00:36:35,151 --> 00:36:39,405
I want Arnaldo to focus
on the upcoming elections.

484
00:36:39,488 --> 00:36:41,574
-Yes, Papa. By all means.
-Okay.

485
00:36:41,657 --> 00:36:42,909
Excuse me.

486
00:36:43,576 --> 00:36:45,995
-Enjoy.
-Thank you.

487
00:36:46,078 --> 00:36:47,246
-Arnaldo.
-Hmm?

488
00:36:47,330 --> 00:36:51,667
Come with me to my meeting with
our people in the gambling den.

489
00:36:52,668 --> 00:36:57,048
They're one of the keys
to securing your success

490
00:36:57,131 --> 00:36:58,591
in the upcoming election.

491
00:36:58,674 --> 00:37:00,927
-Sure. I'll be there.
-Okay.

492
00:37:07,016 --> 00:37:09,852
You're good, kid. I'm impressed.

493
00:37:13,022 --> 00:37:16,776
And in return, I'll give you
and your boss a bonus.

494
00:37:19,654 --> 00:37:21,906
You don't get to say
when I'm getting a bonus.

495
00:37:22,740 --> 00:37:25,701
You might be forgetting
that my boss is your partner.

496
00:37:25,785 --> 00:37:27,870
My boss will take what's rightfully ours,

497
00:37:27,954 --> 00:37:29,288
with or without your blessing.

498
00:37:30,331 --> 00:37:34,085
You probably know that
it's not money my boss is after.

499
00:37:34,627 --> 00:37:38,589
So, what's your boss after?
Tell me, and I'll give you that.

500
00:37:42,969 --> 00:37:45,221
[phone rings]

501
00:37:48,349 --> 00:37:49,600
Boss.

502
00:37:51,352 --> 00:37:52,561
Okay.

503
00:37:53,229 --> 00:37:54,605
My boss wants to talk to you.

504
00:37:59,610 --> 00:38:00,695
Hello.

505
00:38:01,904 --> 00:38:02,989
Yes.

506
00:38:05,741 --> 00:38:09,453
Yes, I heard that
it's not money you want from me.

507
00:38:11,497 --> 00:38:14,542
What do you need? Just tell me.
I can give you that.

508
00:38:19,797 --> 00:38:20,798
[scoffs]

509
00:38:22,049 --> 00:38:25,136
We're on the same side.
Who would have thought?

510
00:38:26,012 --> 00:38:28,222
You want Julio Ardiente's head?

511
00:38:30,182 --> 00:38:32,226
You know, I can give you what you want.

512
00:38:33,102 --> 00:38:35,229
But I'm sorry to say that you're too late.

513
00:38:36,022 --> 00:38:38,316
Because Julio Ardiente's head is mine.

514
00:38:38,774 --> 00:38:41,027
I will kill him myself.

515
00:38:50,328 --> 00:38:54,040
Tell your boss that we need to meet.

516
00:38:54,915 --> 00:38:56,334
We need to talk.

517
00:39:09,096 --> 00:39:10,222
Boss.

518
00:39:13,684 --> 00:39:14,727
Yes.

519
00:39:16,896 --> 00:39:17,897
Okay.

520
00:39:18,981 --> 00:39:23,027
I'll tell Raul that you want
to meet him right away.

521
00:39:36,040 --> 00:39:40,961
You're going to see that man
because you trust him?

522
00:39:43,798 --> 00:39:44,799
No.

523
00:39:46,258 --> 00:39:49,637
Because I don't trust anyone
in this world.

524
00:39:52,556 --> 00:39:57,561
I only need him
to set my plans into motion.

525
00:40:01,816 --> 00:40:04,652
Are you using me too?

526
00:40:06,821 --> 00:40:07,822
Come here.

527
00:40:11,492 --> 00:40:12,868
Natalie, you're different.

528
00:40:15,204 --> 00:40:17,581
You're nothing like those other women.

529
00:40:18,124 --> 00:40:19,917
If it weren't for you,

530
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:21,877
I wouldn't have turned things around.

531
00:40:23,003 --> 00:40:25,047
That's really sweet of you to say.

532
00:40:27,466 --> 00:40:29,093
So…

533
00:40:30,094 --> 00:40:32,096
what are you planning now?

534
00:40:38,686 --> 00:40:39,979
We'll celebrate.

535
00:40:40,771 --> 00:40:43,399
We need to invite every
acquaintance of the Ardientes.

536
00:40:43,482 --> 00:40:45,901
And everyone who worked for them.

537
00:40:47,069 --> 00:40:48,821
We have to gain their trust.

538
00:40:50,448 --> 00:40:53,701
We also need to invest
in the upcoming elections.

539
00:40:54,493 --> 00:40:57,079
And who are we supporting?

540
00:41:00,833 --> 00:41:02,918
My son, Diego, of course.

541
00:41:03,544 --> 00:41:08,340
Because if he wins as governor,
Julio Ardiente will be ousted,

542
00:41:08,799 --> 00:41:10,718
and they'll lose their grip on power.

543
00:41:11,302 --> 00:41:13,095
Their days are numbered.

544
00:41:13,637 --> 00:41:17,016
I will take Emilia's head.

545
00:41:18,726 --> 00:41:20,144
And you…

546
00:41:20,895 --> 00:41:22,646
I'll take Julio's last breath.

547
00:41:30,571 --> 00:41:35,075
[tense music playing]

548
00:41:44,919 --> 00:41:46,045
[phone rings]

549
00:41:48,380 --> 00:41:49,673
[phone rings]

550
00:41:50,758 --> 00:41:53,177
-Emilia?
-Hello, Ivy.

551
00:41:53,469 --> 00:41:57,515
-<i>Are you excited for our dinner?</i>
-Of course.

552
00:41:59,058 --> 00:42:02,019
I am too. I shall see you.

553
00:42:02,561 --> 00:42:05,231
-See you.
-Bye.

554
00:42:16,909 --> 00:42:19,161
So very excited, Emilia.

555
00:42:34,134 --> 00:42:38,847
[suspenseful music playing]

556
00:42:38,931 --> 00:42:40,099
[phone rings]

557
00:42:42,434 --> 00:42:43,519
[phone rings]

558
00:42:45,145 --> 00:42:47,398
-Diego.
<i>-Hello, Ivy.</i>

559
00:42:48,524 --> 00:42:51,944
-How are you?
-I'm fine. Uh…

560
00:42:52,486 --> 00:42:54,655
Emilia and I are having dinner
at the Viento.

561
00:42:55,114 --> 00:42:55,906
Ivy…

562
00:42:58,158 --> 00:42:59,368
Be careful.

563
00:43:00,160 --> 00:43:04,290
Thank you, Diego. Don't worry,
I can handle myself.

564
00:43:04,915 --> 00:43:07,585
-Thanks again.
-All right.

565
00:43:13,173 --> 00:43:17,261
[suspenseful music playing]

566
00:43:24,184 --> 00:43:25,227
[vehicle door opens]

567
00:43:29,815 --> 00:43:30,858
[snaps fingers]

568
00:43:31,275 --> 00:43:32,276
[vehicle door closes]

569
00:43:38,490 --> 00:43:41,243
Go. Fly high, my vulture.

570
00:43:42,661 --> 00:43:47,708
Just make sure that Ivy will be
reduced to a pulp of

571
00:43:47,791 --> 00:43:49,835
rotting flesh the next time I see her.

572
00:43:53,339 --> 00:43:56,467
As you wish, ma'am. We'll take care of it.

573
00:44:03,515 --> 00:44:05,017
Fly high.

574
00:44:18,822 --> 00:44:21,659
Go on, park the car.
You don't have to come with me.

575
00:44:49,395 --> 00:44:50,938
[Emilia humming]

576
00:44:51,021 --> 00:44:56,902
Like a moth in a spider's web.
Goodbye, Ivy Aguas.

577
00:44:57,945 --> 00:45:00,864
[humming]

578
00:45:05,744 --> 00:45:11,208
[humming]

579
00:45:11,291 --> 00:45:13,210
Cheers. [laughs]

580
00:45:33,522 --> 00:45:36,316
Who are you? Where's Emilia?

581
00:45:37,025 --> 00:45:41,780
[suspenseful music playing]

582
00:45:46,535 --> 00:45:49,204
-Where is Emilia?
-[goon laughs]

583
00:45:50,038 --> 00:45:51,415
[goons laughing]

584
00:45:51,790 --> 00:45:53,667
I said, where is Emilia?

585
00:45:57,588 --> 00:45:58,630
[goon laughs]

586
00:46:04,386 --> 00:46:05,471
[grunts]

587
00:46:16,732 --> 00:46:17,816
You!

588
00:46:21,278 --> 00:46:22,029
[growls]

589
00:46:24,490 --> 00:46:26,617
[grunts]

590
00:46:38,086 --> 00:46:39,046
[grunts]

591
00:46:53,352 --> 00:46:56,730
[action music playing]

592
00:47:03,028 --> 00:47:05,197
-[groans]
-[grunts]

593
00:47:07,074 --> 00:47:08,158
[grunts]

594
00:47:12,454 --> 00:47:15,207
-[groans]
-[growls]

595
00:47:17,501 --> 00:47:19,461
[growls]

596
00:47:21,713 --> 00:47:23,298
[groans]

597
00:47:38,605 --> 00:47:39,606
[grunts]

598
00:47:40,357 --> 00:47:41,316
[grunts]

599
00:47:46,196 --> 00:47:47,197
[grunts]

600
00:47:54,037 --> 00:47:58,083
<i>It's either something bad happened to her,</i>
<i>or worse, you're behind all this.</i>

601
00:47:58,166 --> 00:48:02,337
<i>I won't let the Ardientes get away with</i>
<i>the things they do.</i>

602
00:48:02,421 --> 00:48:06,466
<i>So I have to endure everything</i>
<i>no matter what.</i>

603
00:48:06,550 --> 00:48:09,970
<i>I won't file for that damn candidacy</i>
<i>until I find Ivy.</i>

604
00:48:10,053 --> 00:48:12,180
<i>That woman's trying to brainwash you.</i>

605
00:48:12,264 --> 00:48:14,266
<i>I'm on the verge of forgetting</i>
<i>that you're my mother</i>

606
00:48:14,349 --> 00:48:15,767
<i>and slapping your beautiful face!</i>

607
00:48:15,851 --> 00:48:17,978
<i>If something happens to Ivy,</i>
<i>you will answer to me!</i>

608
00:48:18,061 --> 00:48:19,104
<i>Remember that!</i>

609
00:48:19,187 --> 00:48:21,690
<i>You bitch! Stop playing dumb</i>

610
00:48:21,773 --> 00:48:26,361
<i>because I know</i>
<i>you hired those men to rape me!</i>

611
00:48:26,445 --> 00:48:29,156
[theme music fading]
